---
import Analytics from '../../components/Analytics.astro';
const lastUpdated = '10 August 2026';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon-32.png" />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
<title>Privacy Policy — Retail Due Manager</title>
<meta name="description" content="Retail Due Manager's Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use and protect data for retail and wholesale party, invoice, payment and ledger management." />
<meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://zyppi.in/retail-sales-management/privacy-policy" />
<meta name="theme-color" content="#2b5cc4" />
<Analytics />
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #1c2430;
    --muted: #5f6b7a;
    --line: #dde2ea;
    --accent: #2b5cc4;
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --bg-soft: #f7f9fc;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
      Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 24px 80px;
  }
  header.doc-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .mark {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 16px;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 26px;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    margin: 6px 0 32px;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 17px;
    margin: 32px 0 10px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 15px; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 22px; font-size: 15px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .contact-box {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .contact-box p { margin: 4px 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  footer.doc-foot {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="doc-head">
      <span class="mark">RDM</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    </header>
    <p class="updated">Retail Due Manager &middot; Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="card">
      <p>
        Retail Due Manager ("the App," "we," "us," or "our") is a business management
        application that helps retail and wholesale businesses track parties (customers),
        invoices, payments, returns, and account balances. This Privacy Policy explains
        what information the App collects, how it is used and stored, and the choices
        available to you as a user of the App.
      </p>
      <p>
        By using Retail Due Manager, you agree to the practices described in this policy.
        If you do not agree, please do not use the App.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>The App collects and processes the following categories of information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account information.</strong> When you or your team members (Admin/Agent
          accounts) sign in to enable cloud sync, we collect a name, email address, and an
          encrypted password (managed by our authentication provider — we never see or
          store your raw password).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Business data you enter.</strong> This includes the names, phone numbers,
          and addresses of your retail parties/customers, along with invoices, payments,
          returns, credit notes, and ledger entries you create within the App. This data
          belongs to you and is entered voluntarily as part of using the App's core
          bookkeeping features.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local application data.</strong> Settings, backups, and sync-queue
          metadata stored on your device to make the App work offline.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> collect analytics, advertising identifiers, browsing
        behaviour, or any data unrelated to the App's bookkeeping functions. We do not run
        ads and we do not sell data to third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How Your Data Is Stored</h2>
      <p>
        Retail Due Manager is built <strong>offline-first</strong>. All data you enter is
        saved directly on your device in a local database. The App functions fully without
        an internet connection.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose to sign in and enable cloud sync, a copy of your business data is
        also transmitted to and stored on <strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Firebase
        Authentication and Cloud Firestore), used solely as a backup and sync mechanism for
        your own account. This cloud copy is accessible only to accounts you or your
        organization's Admin have registered within the App.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To operate core App features: recording invoices, payments, returns, and
          computing running balances.</li>
        <li>To authenticate Admin and Agent accounts and enforce role-based access within
          your organization.</li>
        <li>To back up and, where enabled, synchronize your data across your own devices.</li>
        <li>To provide customer support if you contact us.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use your business data for advertising, profiling, or any purpose beyond operating the App on your behalf.</p>

      <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        The App uses <strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Authentication and Firestore) as its
        cloud backend for account sign-in and optional data sync. Firebase processes data on
        our behalf under Google's own data-processing and security terms. We do not use any
        other third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking services.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell, rent, or trade your data. Your business data (parties, invoices,
        payments, etc.) is visible only to the Admin and Agent accounts you have registered
        within your own organization inside the App. We do not share your data with
        unrelated third parties, except where required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Your local data remains on your device until you delete it (via the App's data
        management tools) or uninstall the App. Cloud-synced data remains in Firebase until
        you request its deletion. To request deletion of your account and associated cloud
        data, contact us using the details in Section 9 — we will process such requests
        within a reasonable time.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical measures to protect your data, including encrypted
        transmission to Firebase, role-based access control (Admin/Agent permissions) within
        the App, and industry-standard authentication. However, no method of storage or
        transmission is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Retail Due Manager is a business tool intended for use by adults operating a retail
        or wholesale business. It is not directed at, and we do not knowingly collect
        information from, children under 13 years of age.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, wish to access, correct, or delete
        your data, or have any other privacy-related concern, please contact us:
      </p>
      <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:admin@zyppi.in">admin@zyppi.in</a></p>
        <p><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+918918882380">+91 89188 82380</a></p>
      </div>

      <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the App or
        applicable law. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page indicates when this
        policy was last revised. Continued use of the App after changes are posted
        constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="doc-foot">
      &copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} Retail Due Manager. All rights reserved.
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
